      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارتبع</span></b>  <i>He</i> (a. camel) <i>beat</i> [<i>the ground</i>] <i>with
all his legs, in going along;</i> (S;) <i>and went quickly.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also 1, near the end of the paragraph. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He</i> (a man) <i>was of middling stature,
neither tall nor short.</i> (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبَعَ بِالمَكَانِ</span>:
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see 5, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  and 4, near the
end of the paragraph: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبَعَ الحَجَرَ</span>, in
two places, near the end of 1. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارتبع أَمْرَ القَوْمِ</span>
<i>He looked for, expected,</i> or <i>awaited, his being
made commander,</i> or <i>lord, over the people,</i> or
<i>party of men.</i> (TA.)

